spinel: test/share/refuse/attr_assign_value_arg_mutates.rb:8: an attribute assignment in value position (kept, passed on, or a method's last expression, which the method answers) stores into an instance variable that is mutated in place through another name, and its value would be a copy (a String is not yet shared by reference through an assignment's value). Make the assignment a statement of its own, or read the String back through the reader.
